{"title":"llm-gemini 0.38.1","link":"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Nov/20/llm-gemini/","date":1795143717000,"content":"\n    \n        <p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/simonw/llm-gemini/releases/tag/0.38.1\">llm-gemini 0.38.1</a></p>\n        <p>Gemini 4 Carbon only supports <code>low</code>, <code>medium</code> and <code>high</code> reasoning levels - but Gemini 4 Hydrogen and Gemini 4 Neon both have an extra <code>xhigh</code> level.</p>\n<p>I missed that when I added those models to the <code>llm-gemini</code> plugin, which is now fixed in this dot release.</p>\n<p>The <code>xhigh</code> setting for Hydrogen makes a <em>significant</em> difference. I updated my <a href=\"https://static.simonwillison.net/static/2026/gemini-4-carbon-neon-hydrogen-with-xhigh.html\">Gemini 4 comparison grid</a> - note how Hydrogen at high used 5,311 output tokens and cost 3.99 cents, but the same model at xhigh used 31,477 output tokens, cost 23.61 cents, and produced a pelican that's competitive with Gemini 4 Neon:</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Screenshot of a comparison table of illustrations of a pelican riding a bicycle, generated by three models at two thinking levels. Column headers: Thinking, gemini-4-carbon, gemini-4-neon, gemini-4-hydrogen. Row XHIGH: gemini-4-carbon cell is empty and reads &quot;Unsupported&quot;. gemini-4-neon shows a detailed white pelican with a large orange beak riding a red cruiser bicycle along a beachside road, a fish in the wicker basket on the handlebars, with sea, a sailboat, clouds and sun behind, captioned &quot;40 input tokens, 26,546 output = 39.83 cents · 3m 47s&quot;. gemini-4-hydrogen shows a similar pelican on a teal bicycle on a sandy beach with a blue fish in the basket, captioned &quot;40 input tokens, 31,477 output = 23.61 cents · 2m 36s&quot;. Row HIGH: gemini-4-carbon shows a pelican wearing a sailor hat riding a red cruiser bicycle with a fish in the basket beside the sea, captioned &quot;40 input tokens, 20,305 output = 20.31 cents · 4m 11s&quot;. gemini-4-neon shows a pelican on a simpler red bicycle on a dark asphalt road with yellow dashed lines and the sea behind, captioned &quot;40 input tokens, 9,691 output = 14.55 cents · 1m 11s&quot;. gemini-4-hydrogen shows a plainer, flatter pelican on a red bicycle over a green strip of ground with no basket or sea, captioned &quot;40 input tokens, 5,311 output = 3.99 cents · 19s&quot;.\" src=\"/media/e63cbe0ef1b1817cafbcd63803cca860852e1a20c5a632571d6d36bc8e7c77ee.webp\" /></p>\n    \n    \n        <p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/gemini\">gemini</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/llm\">llm</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/llm-reasoning\">llm-reasoning</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/pelican-riding-a-bicycle\">pelican-riding-a-bicycle</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/ai\">ai</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/llms\">llms</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/google\">google</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/generative-ai\">generative-ai</a></p>\n    \n\n","author":"Simon Willison","siteTitle":"Simon Willison’s Weblog","siteHash":"1b599216bd27a00f15d67a3ed9719c64148630c70244b6dd8e743f17cb45527e","entryHash":"af6ef4d85b77b5ab5d77c0050cc4fee6d3b0364575c8e25b1bdbebb2bdb087a2","category":"Tech"}